      "name": "crew_service_quality_issues",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.92,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly targets the query: crew service is a leading driver of recommendation. Categorizing specific issue types (inefficiency, inattentiveness, rudeness, disorganization) gives a genuine axis to group non-recommending flights and prioritize fixes. Sample values are sound reads of the source text — positive reviews correctly map to 'no_service_issue'. No negative-issue samples are shown to verify, but the classification logic is warranted for what is visible."
    },
    {
      "name": "aircraft_modernization",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Aircraft condition is a plausible new axis relating to seat comfort and value, useful for the analysis. However groundedness is weak: sample 1 (no aircraft-age cue in text) is labeled 'modern_new_refurbished' — an unwarranted specific; sample 2 (seats 'dreadful') is labeled 'dated_serviceable' rather than 'old_worn_dirty' despite explicit negative condition language; sample 3 and 5 have no aircraft-age evidence yet get 'dated_serviceable' rather than NULL. It assigns confident condition labels where the text is silent, indicating over-assertion."
    },
    {
      "name": "price_value_alignment",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Value-for-money framing is highly relevant to recommendation and complements the existing 'Value For Money' column with an interpretive categorization rather than mere restatement. Groundedness is mixed: none of the sample reviews mention price at all, yet all five receive confident labels ('justified_premium_worth', 'acceptable_competitive') with almost no NULLs across the whole column (only 1). Assigning price/value verdicts to price-silent rows is an unsupported inference."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.63,
  "rationale": "All three columns give genuine, non-trivial analytical axes (crew issues, aircraft condition, price-value) that are well aligned with the query about improving ratings and recommendations for non-recommending flights, so usefulness is strong. Groundedness is the weaker dimension: 'crew_service_quality_issues' is well grounded on the visible samples, but 'aircraft_modernization' and 'price_value_alignment' both assign confident specific labels to rows whose source text is silent (or, for the dreadful-seats row, contradictory), and the near-total absence of NULLs in price_value_alignment suggests systematic over-assertion rather than correct 'not stated' handling."
}

